WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.830
A second Game of Thrones Season 7 trailer
is out, and there is a heap of cool stuff

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.899
in here – so let’s have a look.

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:12.139
We get some great shots of Dragonstone, the
old island stronghold of the Targaryens where

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:14.760
Daenerys has finally arrived.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:20.380
Dragonstone looks way crazier in the books,
with huge stone dragons, and hundreds of gargoyles.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:26.060
It’s also a volcanic island, with caves
full of obsidian , or dragonglass – one

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.590
of the only materials known that can kill
white walkers.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.930
So Dragonstone’s obsidian should be really
important this season.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.540
Dragonstone was held by the Targaryens for
centuries, until Robert Baratheon took over

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.010
and gave the island to his brother Stannis
– this is Stannis’ banner here.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:47.239
But now Stannis is dead, and Dany’s arrived,
it’s time to redecorate.

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:52.100
Dany takes down the banner, symbolically returning
the castle to her family.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:57.230
She again looks over the Painted Table map
of Westeros, representing her plans to conquer

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:58.610
the kingdoms.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:03.660
We also see Dany’s dragon Drogon, who’s
huge now – look how tiny Dany is perched

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.660
on his back.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.799
Drogon’s looking a lot like Balerion the
Black Dread, the famous dragon of Aegon the

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:13.639
Conqueror , who first took Westeros three
hundred years ago.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:17.850
Dany is very much walking in her ancestor’s
footsteps.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:21.719
To take Westeros though, Dany’s gotta sail
from Dragonstone to the mainland.

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:26.499
Which should be easy – but we see she’s
attacked at sea by Euron Greyjoy.

00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:31.520
And Euron doesn’t play fair – he uses
some explosive fiery weapon against Dany’s

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.520
fleet, which Yara and Theon aren’t too keen
on.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:39.390
Yara leaps into battle cause she’s Yara
fucking Greyjoy, while Theon stands and looks

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.429
upset because he’s Theon fucking Greyjoy.

00:01:42.429 --> 00:01:47.259
Theon at least does survive – we see him
collapsing on a beach, like in Planet of the

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:52.380
Apes . But it looks like this battle goes
well for Euron, because we then see him sailing

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.729
in to King’s Landing – this red smudge
on the Greyjoy kraken on his sails might represent

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:03.549
Euron’s heraldry in the books – a red
eye with a crown and crows . Euron might have

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:05.659
come to visit Queen Cersei.

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:10.379
Maybe he’s being welcomed to the city in
this shot – or maybe someone else, it’s

00:02:10.379 --> 00:02:11.379
hard to say.

00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:16.130
Either way, the relationship between Euron
and Cersei could be a big deal this season.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:21.569
Cersei, for her part, is standing in what
looks to be the basement of the Red Keep,

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:25.540
where they keep the old Targaryen dragon skulls
from years ago.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:30.150
Maybe Cersei has finally realised that Daenerys
and her dragons are a threat, and is trying

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.680
to work how to slay dragons.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.070
For the record, dragons in Game of Thrones
have been killed with scorpion bolts , arrows

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:41.599
, even angry peasants when they’re trapped
indoors . So Dany’s dragons can definitely

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:45.769
be killed, and there’s also the possibility
they might be magically mind controlled – by

00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:51.610
someone like Bran or Bloodraven or Euron in
the books – or even by the Night King.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:56.610
So Dany’s dragons are powerful, but shit
can and probably will happen to them.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.890
For now, though, Dany and her dragons are
kicking ass.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:05.000
We see a huge battle, with Dany on Drogon
with Dothraki attacking some Lannister soldiers

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.140
including Jaime and Bronn.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.801
Things get hot and heavy what with all the
dragonfire, which is reminiscent of a huge

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:15.519
battle from Aegon’s Conquest called the
Field of Fire – when the Targaryens used

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:20.299
three dragons to roast thousands of men on
the battlefield . So these Lannister chumps’ll

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:23.050
be barbequed, but – what about Jaime?

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:27.049
We see him charging across the burning field
– who’s he attacking?

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:29.370
Surely not Dany and her dragons, right?

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.319
He’d be eaten alive!

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:36.470
Then again, Jaime in the books believes he
“cannot die while Cersei lives” – that

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:40.840
the twins will “die together as [they] were
born together” . There are some amazing

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.890
theories here, which we’ll cover in a Cersei
video soon.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.200
But yeah this battle looks pretty crazy.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.780
We see Grey Worm have a moment with Missandei
before a battle between Dany’s Unsullied

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.950
and the Lannisters.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:58.219
It’s possible this castle they’re attacking
is Casterly Rock, a huge Lannister fortress

00:03:58.219 --> 00:04:02.849
– and it’s interesting that these Unsullied
seem to be opening this gate from inside.

00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:04.889
How’d they get in?

00:04:04.889 --> 00:04:07.400
This might be a plan worked out by Tyrion.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.139
Cause Tyrion grew up in Casterly Rock, this
was his home.

00:04:11.139 --> 00:04:15.709
And when Tyrion was sixteen, his father Tywin
put him in “charge of all the drains and

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:20.770
cisterns” there . Maybe Tyrion knows some
back entrances into the Rock – so Grey Worm

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:26.290
can get in all sneaky loike and open the gates
from within – kinda like how Dany took Meereen

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:30.910
. So yeah with Tyrion’s tricks on their
side, Dany might just capture the Lannisters

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.530
strongest castle.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.730
Cersei will not be pleased.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:38.940
By the way, we see Jaime walking around some
unfamiliar castle, and there’s a dead guy

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.110
on the ground.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.560
Did Jaime just lead some attack?

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.560
On who?

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:47.850
This could maybe be Highgarden, the seat of
the Tyrells, who along with the Sand Snakes

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.440
are Dany’s allies against Cersei.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.570
Again it’s ominous that these guys aren’t
in the trailer.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:58.450
Further north, we see Arya riding, probably
to Winterfell, to finally reunite with her

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:04.170
long lost family – Sansa and Jon Snow, who
haven’t seen Arya other since Season 1.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:08.900
Jon and Arya especially were really close
early on, so it’ll be a hugely emotional

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:14.170
moment for the Starks to get back together
, after all they’ve been through.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:17.320
Littlefinger, meanwhile, still seems to be
trying to divide them.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.070
He says some nonsense about “Fight[ing]
every battle, everywhere.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.070
Always.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.950
In your mind”, which means…

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.270
something?

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:29.480
Littlefinger seems to think himself very clever,
but his whole plan seems to hinge on Sansa

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:34.700
betraying her family for him – which probably
will not happen given that Sansa in the trailer

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:40.020
says “When the snows fall and the white
winds blow, the lone wolf dies but the pack

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.400
survives”.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:46.420
This is what Ned tells Arya way back in Book
1, and it’s about Stark solidarity, sticking

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.330
together to survive.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.100
So Sansa won’t listen to Littlefinger.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:54.750
In fact, promo shots have shown Arya wearing
the Valyrian steel dagger that Littlefinger

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.590
used to betray Ned Stark.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:06:01.740
So some fans speculate that Arya and Sansa
will kill Littlefinger with his own blade,

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.520
to avenge the death and destruction he brought
on their family.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.330
Another Stark, Bran, passes through the Wall
with Meera, and it looks like he too arrives

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:11.620
at Winterfell.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:16.660
Here he is in the godswood with some new wheels
– so much has since he was last here.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:21.380
It’s not clear who the guy standing next
to him is – maybe Davos, or Maester Wolkan,

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:24.200
or like a Obi-Wan force-ghost of Bloodraven?

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.430
Hard to say.

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:29.770
Either way, Bran’s psychic powers will be
a really big deal this season.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:34.190
For one thing, Bran now knows that Jon Snow’s
mother is Lyanna Stark, so that’ll be a

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:39.830
big truth bomb – though the next logical
question will be – who’s Jon’s dad ? Also

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:45.370
at Winterfell are Brienne and Podrick – name
a more iconic duo, I’ll wait.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:49.660
We see Jon venture north with an all-star
team of warriors, including Tormund, and the

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.040
Hound, and Beric Dondarrion with his flaming
sword.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.290
There are million reasons why this team is
the coolest thing ever.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:07:00.990
Some of the greatest fighters alive, from
opposite sides brought together.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:06.010
Sandor and Beric fought before, in fact Sandor
killed Beric – then he was resurrected.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:10.700
Beric was resurrected, Jon was resurrected,
everyone thought the Hound was dead before

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.050
he was metaphorically reborn.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:18.900
This is almost a team of the walking dead,
fighting the walking dead – cause they battle

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:22.740
the zombies, the wights, controlled by the
white walkers.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.720
Fans have pointed out that scene looks a bit
like the story of the “last hero” from

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.210
the books, who’s said to have fought the
walkers thousands of years ago.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:36.610
Apparently, the hero “set out into the dead
lands with a sword, a horse, a dog, and [twelve]

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:37.610
companions”.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:43.290
And there are twelve companions in this shot
– Jon has his sword Longclaw, and his dog

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.320
could be Ghost – or maybe the Hound.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:50.790
In the story, the last hero’s friends were
killed, along with his horse and his dog – he

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:55.580
even lost his sword . Maybe that’s what’s
happening in these shots of Jon – he’s

00:07:55.580 --> 00:08:00.330
still got a horse and a sword, but he’s
alone – have Tormund Sandor and Beric been

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.470
killed?

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:05.790
In the story of the “last hero”, the hero
is almost caught by the walkers, but is saved

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:10.530
by the children of the forest – those mysterious
forest hippies who hung out with Bloodraven

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:15.830
. The analogue here might be for Jon to be
saved by Bran’s magic – we see ravens

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:19.830
flying over the army of the dead, one with
white eyes.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:25.280
The birds are being magically controlled by
Bran, he might use them to attack the walkers,

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.770
maybe to save Jon – though he might be too
late to help Jon’s companions.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:35.960
Bran warging a bird is a fulfilment of what
Bloodraven tells him in Dance – that Bran

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:40.810
will “never walk again”, but he “will
fly” . It’s tragic that Bran was robbed

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:45.010
of his ability to walk – he wanted to be
a knight as a child.

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:48.370
But magic gives him to power to do something
even higher.

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:53.870
A complication, though, might be the connection
between Bran and the Night King.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.900
We still don’t really know the meaning of
this mark that the King left on Bran, but

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:02.820
it seems to suggest some connection between
the two, like some Harry Potter Voldemort

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:03.820
shit.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:09.440
We might see some intense psychic battles
between Bran and the Night King this season.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.470
So there is huge stuff happening in the north
and in the south, amidst ice and fire.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:19.580
But there’s one more thing that might happen
that could be the greatest moment of all.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:25.200
We get a shot of what looks like the Hound,
somewhere in the south, maybe in King’s

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:29.360
Landing – which just happens to be where
the Mountain is.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.360
Sandor and Gregor Clegane are brothers, remember.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:36.650
Years ago, Gregor gave Sandor the burns that
disfigured his face, and they’ve hated each

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.050
other ever since.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:41.810
They’ve both changed dramatically over the
series.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:46.690
Sandor was symbolically reborn, while Gregor
was quite literally reanimated.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:50.930
Fans have speculated for years that these
brothers will clash in the greatest Westerosi

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:55.890
grudge match imaginable, a combat commonly
called Cleganebowl.

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:57.070
[AIRHORNS].

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:02.980
It’s kinda dumb and prolly won’t happen,
but man it would be quite cool.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:03.980
Anyway.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:08.760
This season is gonna be crazy, with heaps
of long-awaited moments – Dany at Dragonstone,

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:13.570
Euron on the attack, dragons in battle, the
fall of the Rock, Stark family reunion, Bran

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:18.360
finally flies, and winter arrives at last.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.360
Thanks for watching.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:23.590
Like and subscribe for more videos, and thanks
to the Patrons for making this possible, including

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:29.130
Jalal Ghazaleen, Lars Larsson, "Boots" Davies,
WatcherOfTheShift, Sofia Fernandez, dbnoodle

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:30.130
and Daz.

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:30.589
Cheers.

